<title>USA: Indiana $41 mln agency deal ylds 6.35 pct in 2026.</title>
<headline>Indiana $41 mln agency deal ylds 6.35 pct in 2026.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-09-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>PaineWebber Inc said Wednesday it tentatively priced $41.2 million Indiana housing Finance Authority bonds at a top yield of 6.35 percent in 2026.</p>
<p>The preliminary pricing follows:</p>
<p>INDIANA HOUSING FINANCE AUTHORITY</p>
<p>RE: $41,185,000*</p>
<p>SINGLE FAMILY MORTGAGE REVENUE BONDS</p>
<p>1996 SERIES D-1 (NON-AMT) AND D-2 (AMT)</p>
<p>THIS IS A PRELIMINARY PRICING.</p>
<p>THIS ISSUE WILL BE IN BOOK ENTRY FORM THROUGH THE FACILITIES OF DTC</p>
<p>					    15,415,000*</p>
<p>					 SERIES D-1 NON AMT</p>
<p>    MOODY'S: Aaa		   S&amp;P: NR</p>
<p>    DATED: 09/15/1996	  FIRST COUPON: 07/01/1997</p>
<p>DUE: 07/01 &amp; 01/01</p>
<p>ALL BONDS ARE PRICED AT PAR.</p>
